<b>Subject:</b> Technical Inquiry Regarding FSM Controller Specifications</=
span><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<p class=3D"xxmsonormal">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<p class=3D"xxmsonormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:black">Dear =
AOS Team,</span><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<p class=3D"xxmsonormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:black">I hop=
e this email finds you well.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<p class=3D"xxmsonormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:black">Follo=
wing the quotation we recently received from your team, I am writing to you=
 as the Head of the Control Department at ARC. We are currently reviewing t=
he proposal to integrate your Fast Steering
 Mirror (FSM) systems into our upcoming project, and before finalizing our =
decision, we would like to clarify a few technical aspects regarding the co=
ntroller.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<p class=3D"xxmsonormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:black">Speci=
fically, we would appreciate it if you could provide more information, docu=
mentation, or datasheets covering the following points:</span><o:p></o:p></=
p>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt" id=3D"x_x_p-rc_43dfc9d3dbec0b3a-73">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:black;mso-list:l15 level1 lfo3"><b=
><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Communication Interfaces:</span></b><span=
 style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> Aside from the digital Ethernet interface ment=
ioned in your documentation, what other
 communication protocols, industrial buses, or APIs are supported by the co=
ntroller?</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<li class=3D"xxmsolistparagraph" style=3D"margin-left:0in;mso-list:l12 leve=
l2 lfo4"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:#0070C0">The FSM controller =
can also receive position commands using SPI and RS485 interfaces.&nbsp; Th=
e Ethernet communication interface is intended
 to be a supervisory and configuration interface and is not typically used =
as the real-time command interface.&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt" id=3D"x_x_p-rc_43dfc9d3dbec0b3a-74">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:black;mso-list:l5 level1 lfo5"><b>=
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Bandwidth and Tuning:</span></b><span styl=
e=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> How flexible is the adjustable bandwidth via the di=
gital Ethernet interface, and what specific
 tools or software are provided for real-time loop tuning and performance m=
onitoring?</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l6 level2 lfo6"><=
span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">The FSM Controller GUI provides full contro=
l of the internal control settings with configurable parameters, allowing f=
or complete bandwidth control within the
 total performance envelope of the FSM, as well as flexible filtering at mu=
ltiple points in the control chain:</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"square">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l3 level3 lfo7"><=
span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Proportional, Integral, and Derivative gain=
 coefficients for X and Y axis</span><o:p></o:p></li><li class=3D"xxmsonorm=
al" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l3 level3 lfo7"><span style=3D"font-siz=
e:11.0pt">Position sensor input 2<sup>nd</sup>-order biquad filter coeffici=
ents</span><o:p></o:p></li><li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0=
;mso-list:l3 level3 lfo7"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Derivative branc=
h 2<sup>nd</sup>-order biquad filter coefficients</span><o:p></o:p></li><li=
 class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l3 level3 lfo7"><spa=
n style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Two cascaded controller output filter 2<sup>nd=
</sup>-order biquad coefficients</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
</ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l17 level2 lfo8">=
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">The FSM Controller GUI can command the FSM=
 to execute the following characterization tests and retrieve 4-second long=
 full-rate 500kHz logs for out-of-band
 analysis:</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"square">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l8 level3 lfo9"><=
span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Standard &#8211; No additional position cha=
nges are enacted, useful for viewing the performance of the FSM with the po=
sition caged or uncaged.&nbsp; The controller can
 be configured to inject a frequency or white noise disturbance during this=
 characterization test as well.</span><o:p></o:p></li><li class=3D"xxmsonor=
mal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l8 level3 lfo9"><span style=3D"font-si=
ze:11.0pt">Step Response &#8211; Configurable Start and End positions in bo=
th X and Y axes, step command is executed at approximately 400ms into the 4=
s log</span><o:p></o:p></li><li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C=
0;mso-list:l8 level3 lfo9"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Frequency Sweep=
 &#8211; Using Direct Digital Synthesis built-in to the FSM electronics, on=
e can specify a start and end frequency and the controller will inject eith=
er
 position commands or a disturbance with the frequency sweep.</span><o:p></=
o:p></li><li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l8 level=
3 lfo9"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Open-loop command pulse &#8211; Al=
lows for an at-rest FSM to be &#8220;shoved&#8221; by an open loop command =
pulse to derive impulse response in-system</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
</ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l11 level2 lfo10"=
><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">The FSM Controller GUI includes a self-tu=
ne procedure which executes full-rate-logged step responses and analyzes th=
e rise-time, settle-time, and overshoot
 to determine a performance metric and then automatically performs stochast=
ic axial search to optimize P, I, and D gains for X and Y controller parame=
ters.&nbsp; We have found this automated process greatly reduces manual lab=
or time tuning a FSM in-situ.</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:black;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo11"><b=
><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Software Integration &amp; Examples:</spa=
n></b><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> Do you provide sample code, softwar=
e development kits (SDKs), or integration examples
 (such as Python, C++, or LabVIEW scripts) to interface with the controller=
?</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l1 level2 lfo12">=
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">We have an example FSM Controller GUI deve=
loped in Visual Studio in C# that implements the Ethernet connection and pr=
ovides access to the data structures that
 drive all of the configuration parameters.</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:black;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo13"><b=
><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Hardware &amp; I/O Specifications:</span>=
</b><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> What are the exact power supply requi=
rements (voltage/current) for the controller
 unit, and what type of physical connectors are used for inputs, outputs, a=
nd sensor feedback?</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l13 level2 lfo14"=
><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">The bare FSM controller electronics requi=
res +28VDC with a supported transient current (for large, fast steps) of 10=
A. Quiescent current with the FSM caged
 and stationary tends to hover around 400mA.</span><o:p></o:p></li><li clas=
s=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l13 level2 lfo14"><span s=
tyle=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Standard interfaces are listed below:</span><o:p>=
</o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"square">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l16 level3 lfo15"=
><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">+28VDC Power: 4-pin Mate-N-LOK connector =
or supplied via backplane and converted from 120VAC in 3U chassis configura=
tion</span><o:p></o:p></li><li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0=
;mso-list:l16 level3 lfo15"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Sensor and Dri=
ve: 15-pin DSUB</span><o:p></o:p></li><li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"co=
lor:#0070C0;mso-list:l16 level3 lfo15"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">RS4=
85: 9-pin DSUB</span><o:p></o:p></li><li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"col=
or:#0070C0;mso-list:l16 level3 lfo15"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">SPI:=
 Backplane</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:black;mso-list:l9 level1 lfo16"><b=
><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Latency and Determinism:</span></b><span =
style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> What is the internal processing latency of the =
digital controller, and does it support
 real-time deterministic operation for high-speed jitter rejection?</span><=
o:p></o:p></li></ul>
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"disc">
<ul style=3D"margin-top:0in" type=3D"circle">
<li class=3D"xxmsonormal" style=3D"color:#0070C0;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo17">=
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">All digital control is implemented in the =
FGPA and is completely deterministic.&nbsp; The tightly-coupled ARM process=
or and Ethernet are strictly supervisory/configuration
 interfaces</span><o:p></o:p></li></ul>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<p class=3D"xxmsonormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:black">To en=
sure we have a complete understanding of how the system will integrate into=
 our existing control architecture, would it be possible to schedule a brie=
f technical meeting with one of your
 engineers next week to discuss these details?</span><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<p class=3D"xxmsonormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:black">Thank=
 you for your continued support and assistance. I look forward to hearing f=
rom you.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">
<p class=3D"xxmsonormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;color:black">Best =
regards,</span><o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
